 "text": "Hi, nice to hear from you. How are you? Put it in a sealed bag with cold water when you get home, and leave it in the coolest part of the kitchen. Both work, but ice cubes melt faster. A block of cheese or loaf of bread is the easiest way to keep everything cold. Keep the cooler out of the sun, and don't put anything hot right next to it, like leftovers from the grill. Tell him it' for the whole weekend. He' appreciate it. Yes, empty it, and fill it with fresh cold water from the tap.",
